before:
An outline can mark focus without changing the element’s box size.
```css
input:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid purple;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

after:
`:hover` matches when a pointer is over a part.

```css
a:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}
```

This underlines a link while a pointer is over it. A person using only a keyboard may never trigger hover.

An outline can show focus without changing the space the control takes up.

```css
input:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid navy;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

The outline is 3 pixels wide, solid, and navy. The offset leaves a 2-pixel gap between the control and the outline.

`:disabled` chooses an unavailable control.

```css
button:disabled {
  opacity: 0.6;
}
```

`opacity` controls how see-through it looks. The HTML `disabled` attribute makes the button unavailable. Lower opacity alone does not disable it.
